  ],
  "art_inventory": {
   "named": 8,
   "joinable_to_an_event": 4,
   "named_but_unmatched": 4,
   "opaque_unnameable": 19,
   "marquee_sized_in_store": 27,
   "store_note": "all are 600x120, verified by re-counting the store (8 named HomeBanner_<id>.png in the client's cache + 19 more in static_banner/ under opaque ids such as 3663_20240829042016.png). 19 of the opaque filenames embed a timestamp (3197_20230905013503, the 3658..3665_2024082x cluster) -- a lead, not a date.",
   "opaque_verdict_2026_10_01": "RESOLVED, in the negative, by LOOKING at all 19 (contact sheet, 600x120 as measured): they are NOT marquee banners. 18 are the SHOP bundle promos (Bundle of Replenishment, Daily Recharge Bundle, Transcension Pearl Bundle, ...) under static_banner/bundle/, and 1 is a LOGIN bonus banner (October Daily Rewards) under static_banner/login/. They share the marquee's 600x120 shape, which is why they read as marquee-sized, and that shape is the whole of the case for them. Consequence: the real marquee art pool is the 8 NAMED banners and nothing else, so with_art 4 + promos 4 = 8 is the CEILING, not a floor -- and the audit's open question (could a non-MST index map 2+ of the opaque 19 to marquee-class events, which would make the totals wrong?) is answered NO by the images themselves.",
   "not_verifiable_by_check": "--check cannot see these drift: they are measured by re-reading the store (--verify-art), not derived from the corpus.",
   "verify_with": "python3 harness/gen_banner_campaigns.py --verify-art"
  },
  "caveats": [
   "Everything in `events` is [Community] data from the Exvius Fandom wiki: a HINT, not verification, and NOT shipped game data. The shipped tables carry no dates at all, so an era window can only come from here or be authored.",
   "art: null means the EVENT IS KNOWN AND DATED BUT THE ART IS LOST from what we hold. It is not a gap in this table; recovering it is a collection problem and is deliberately out of scope here.",
   "end: null is a SECOND, SEPARATE gap from art, and it is the binding one for serving: the marquee's `_canTransit` needs an end, so a null end means an authored value, not a servable window. Roughly half the table is in that state -- see `totals.end_null`. Do not read 'with art' as 'servable'.",
   "The class filter is a SELECTION and reports its own size: see `totals.dropped_by_class` for how many Global records it removed, and `totals.dropped_unclassified` for records carrying no event class. The filter's justification is that all four title-matched banners are Story/Raid/Series events, but note what that does NOT prove -- the other four banners the client holds are summon-promotion art, and the marquee DID carry summon promos (DailyVideoSummon2 has banner version 49 in the client's own cache index). So the class filter describes the events we can NAME, not the full set the marquee ever ran.",
   "The corpus mislabels some records (DRAGON QUEST The Adventure of Dai is tagged `Ranked Event`), so the filter inherits noise it cannot detect and does not attempt to.",
   "The 8th Anniversary is `region=jp` only in this corpus (Daily 8th Anniversary Celebration Quest, 2023-09-22); there is no Global record, so no 8th-anniversary event can appear in an era.",
   "The community corpus ends 2024-08; Global Season 4 runs to 2024-10-30, so the last two months of the client's own era are simply absent rather than filtered out.",
   "Several events ran more than once. Each run is its own record and its own era month; art attaches to the run the corpus marks `preferred`, so a re-run month shows art: null by design."
  ]
 },
